WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:03.036
-We were talking, during the
break, about remote learning

00:00:03.036 --> 00:00:04.170 line:92%
I got a 2- and a 4-year-old.

00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:04.871 line:92%
There is not a lot of it.

00:00:04.871 --> 00:00:06.539 align:start size:94% position:6%
How is your 10-year-old doin
and are you helpful?

00:00:06.539 --> 00:00:09.376 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, I mean, well,
here's what's terrifying

00:00:09.376 --> 00:00:10.210 line:92%
is she does remote learning,

00:00:10.210 --> 00:00:13.246
so there's social studies,
there's English, there's art

00:00:13.246 --> 00:00:16.883 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I'm always happy to hop in
and help her out.

00:00:16.883 --> 00:00:20.553 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then when I see her coming
at me with her math sheets

00:00:20.553 --> 00:00:23.790 align:start size:94% position:6%
I cringe because it's become
very clear

00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:26.626 size:84% position:42%
to both me and my wife
that our math knowledge

00:00:26.626 --> 00:00:28.561 align:start size:94% position:6%
kind of topped out
in third grade

00:00:28.561 --> 00:00:30.430 align:start size:94% position:6%
and hers is at
a fourth-grade level.

00:00:30.430 --> 00:00:32.866 align:start size:94% position:6%
And there are literally --
I just have this thing

00:00:32.866 --> 00:00:35.902
we downloaded called the Tin
Math Pack, and I'm trying --

00:00:35.902 --> 00:00:39.406
I downloaded my own so I can d
it and then check her answers.

00:00:39.406 --> 00:00:42.308
And I realize I don't know
how to do these new things

00:00:42.308 --> 00:00:47.113
where it's called the bar method
for solving --

00:00:47.113 --> 00:00:48.515 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Oh, no.

00:00:48.515 --> 00:00:50.917 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm like, "I don't know how
this works."

00:00:50.917 --> 00:00:52.052 line:92%
And I'm going to get this wrong.

00:00:52.052 --> 00:00:55.188
So I'm terrified that she'
going to come to me and go

00:00:55.188 --> 00:00:55.889 size:81% position:41% line:92%
"Can we go over this?"

00:00:55.889 --> 00:00:57.690 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm like, "I kind of
don't know what this" --

00:00:57.690 --> 00:01:00.226 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I'm trying to
find YouTube videos.

00:01:00.226 --> 00:01:03.897 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. I can't believe
how ignorant I am

00:01:03.897 --> 00:01:06.132 align:start size:94% position:6%
that it never occurred to me
that there would be

00:01:06.132 --> 00:01:09.102 align:start size:94% position:6%
a different way to teach peopl
the same stuff.

00:01:09.102 --> 00:01:12.272
-Exact-- Well, apparently
that happened in the '60s

00:01:12.272 --> 00:01:14.607 align:start size:94% position:6%
with new math,
but now the new math

00:01:14.607 --> 00:01:16.509 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you and I grew up on
is old.

00:01:16.509 --> 00:01:18.878 size:78% position:39%
And there's something
called Singapore math

00:01:18.878 --> 00:01:20.880 align:start size:94% position:6%
and there's something called
the bar method.

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:22.916 line:92%
There's all these new methods.

00:01:22.916 --> 00:01:24.150 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I have no idea.

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:25.885 size:88% position:44% line:92%
I don't know what to do.

00:01:25.885 --> 00:01:29.522
-Oh, it's good to look ahead and
realize that's the frustration

00:01:29.522 --> 00:01:31.157 align:start size:94% position:6%
that's coming down the pik
for me.

00:01:31.157 --> 00:01:33.693 line:92%
-It is coming, so get ready.

00:01:33.693 --> 00:01:35.161 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It's -- Oh, boy.

00:01:35.161 --> 00:01:38.498 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I just want to say that you
hosted the Webby Awards

00:01:38.498 --> 00:01:39.833 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
on Tuesday night.

00:01:39.833 --> 00:01:42.769 align:start size:94% position:6%
I actually hosted that sho
a few years ago.

00:01:42.769 --> 00:01:43.403 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It's a ton of fun.

00:01:43.403 --> 00:01:46.906
I, of course, did it live
when there was an audience

00:01:46.906 --> 00:01:49.542
I think this is a thing a lot of
comedians are figuring out

00:01:49.542 --> 00:01:51.978 align:start size:94% position:6%
How will this sort of
virtual entertainment work

00:01:51.978 --> 00:01:54.180 align:start size:94% position:6%
Did you still have
a good time doing it?

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:55.582 line:92%
-I had a good time recording it.

00:01:55.582 --> 00:01:57.684 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, I hosted it
three times live.

00:01:57.684 --> 00:01:59.319 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Gotcha.
-And you're right.

00:01:59.319 --> 00:02:01.554 size:81% position:41% line:92%
It is such a fun show.

00:02:01.554 --> 00:02:02.255 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It's really goofy.

00:02:02.255 --> 00:02:03.656 align:start size:94% position:6%
It doesn't take itself
seriously.

00:02:03.656 --> 00:02:08.061 align:start size:94% position:6%
And now, I'm scrambling
to catch up

00:02:08.061 --> 00:02:09.863 align:start size:94% position:6%
with the technology
that's needed.

00:02:09.863 --> 00:02:10.830 line:92%
So there was a lot of things

00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:13.600 size:88% position:44%
There was a lot of texts
that needed to be read.

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:16.503 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I had to keep looking,
because I don't have --

00:02:16.503 --> 00:02:19.272 size:84% position:42%
I couldn't figure out
teleprompter technology

00:02:19.272 --> 00:02:22.442 align:start size:94% position:6%
and proper lighting,
so I did the best job I could.

00:02:22.442 --> 00:02:26.279 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I hope that historically
people will look at

00:02:26.279 --> 00:02:28.515 align:start size:94% position:6%
the 2020 Webbys and go,
"This has a real

00:02:28.515 --> 00:02:30.783 align:start size:94% position:6%
post-apocalyptic wasteland fee
to it."

00:02:30.783 --> 00:02:35.855
Which might be a good historical
document for this is the time.

00:02:35.855 --> 00:02:37.357 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I hope
if they ever ask me again

00:02:37.357 --> 00:02:39.592 align:start size:94% position:6%
I will be a little
more up to speed with --

00:02:39.592 --> 00:02:41.060 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because it especially
celebrates people

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:43.062 align:start size:94% position:6%
that are doing amazing thing
on the Web.

00:02:43.062 --> 00:02:45.165 align:start size:94% position:6%
So a lot of it just
looked great.

00:02:45.165 --> 00:02:47.400 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then they cut back to
Grandpa Oswalt.

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:51.538 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Is it on? I don't see?
Hello? Okay."

00:02:51.538 --> 00:02:55.675
Like, it's just this weird
multi-generational thing.

00:02:55.675 --> 00:02:57.644 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know?
-Yeah.

00:02:57.644 --> 00:02:58.211 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-A little weird.

00:02:58.211 --> 00:03:01.915 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's so true that so much wor
is going to be timestamped

00:03:01.915 --> 00:03:06.986
in a way that will make it ver
clear when anybody looks back,

00:03:06.986 --> 00:03:10.223 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Oh, that?
That was during that?"

00:03:10.223 --> 00:03:12.892 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I have gone down
the saddest rabbit hole

00:03:12.892 --> 00:03:14.727 align:start size:94% position:6%
where I will go
online to YouTube.

00:03:14.727 --> 00:03:16.262 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't know
if you're doing this, too.

00:03:16.262 --> 00:03:18.598 align:start size:94% position:6%
People have posted videos
for years now

00:03:18.598 --> 00:03:21.467 align:start size:94% position:6%
of huge, like, summer
blockbusters, the big moments,

00:03:21.467 --> 00:03:23.436 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they will
record the audience

00:03:23.436 --> 00:03:26.339 align:start size:94% position:6%
cheering for big moments.
-Oh, wow.

00:03:26.339 --> 00:03:30.276
-A guy recorded opening night of
"Avengers: Endgame,"

00:03:30.276 --> 00:03:31.811 align:start size:94% position:6%
all the big moments
when Captain America

00:03:31.811 --> 00:03:35.248
goes "Avengers, assemble" or
when he picks up Thor's hammer

00:03:35.248 --> 00:03:39.252
all those where the crowd is
just "Yeah!" like, freaking out,

00:03:39.252 --> 00:03:43.523 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I'm watching all of thes
with this sad, like --

00:03:43.523 --> 00:03:46.726 align:start size:94% position:6%
remember people just out
cheering for stuff.

00:03:46.726 --> 00:03:50.597 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm watching all this --
and I used to despise

00:03:50.597 --> 00:03:51.831 line:92%
people in movies filming things.

00:03:51.831 --> 00:03:55.969
Now I thank God that people were
there recording the audience

00:03:55.969 --> 00:03:59.239 align:start size:94% position:6%
because it's like this age
that's gone now.

00:03:59.239 --> 00:04:00.173 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:04:00.173 --> 00:04:02.041 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And now there's like
whole videos put together,

00:04:02.041 --> 00:04:04.611 align:start size:94% position:6%
like best audience reactions o
"Deadpool,"

00:04:04.611 --> 00:04:05.445 line:92%
best audience reactions of -

00:04:05.445 --> 00:04:07.480 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I'm just watching all this
stuff, and it's amazing.

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:09.549 align:start size:94% position:6%
-What a funny thing
that you're right, that I thin

00:04:09.549 --> 00:04:13.119
we all wanted the moviegoing
experience to completely make us

00:04:13.119 --> 00:04:14.887 align:start size:94% position:6%
forget that we were
watching it with other people.

00:04:14.887 --> 00:04:17.624
And now, of course, that's
the thing you miss the most.

00:04:17.624 --> 00:04:19.892 align:start size:94% position:6%
Patton, it's always
so lovely to talk to you.

00:04:19.892 --> 00:04:22.362 size:84% position:42%
Stay safe and healthy,
and we'll see you soon,

00:04:22.362 --> 00:04:23.029 size:75% position:38% line:92%
hopefully in person.

00:04:23.029 --> 00:04:26.633 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, hopefully in person,
alright, man, be safe.

